  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# One-on-one: Nina and Oliver\n\n**Date:** May 18\n**Attendees:** Nina Castellanos, Oliver Brandt\n\n## Summary\n\nFortnightly one-on-one. We covered the Harbourline retest plan, Oliver's promotion packet, and how he wants to handle the next few weeks at home before his leave.\n\n## Work\n\n- The Harbourline beta milestone slipped a week because the account-linking screen is being reworked after the first round of testing. Oliver is comfortable with the new date and has told the client.\n- Oliver's promotion packet to senior designer is nearly ready. He wants one more case study in it, ideally the Harbourline onboarding work once the retest is done.\n- I agreed to review the draft packet before the next calibration round.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Nina Castellanos** — review Oliver's promotion packet by May 29 and send written feedback.\n- **Oliver Brandt** — add the Harbourline onboarding case study to the packet after the retest.\n\n## Home and family\n\n- Oliver asked to keep Fridays short for the next month. Their son Leo has swimming lessons straight after school, and Oliver and Maya take turns collecting him.\n- Oliver and Maya's daughter Ivy is starting nursery in September; Maya is handling the settling-in sessions.\n- Ivy turns five on June 2 and they are having a small party at home that weekend. Oliver will be offline that Friday afternoon.\n- Oliver is the parent of both Leo and Ivy, and Maya is their mother; worth remembering for scheduling around school holidays.\n\n## Wellbeing\n\nOliver said the workload feels manageable now that the Harbourline scope is settled. He is looking forward to the Lisbon trip and has already started the handover notes for Sam.\n\n## Next one-on-one\n\nIn two weeks, after the Harbourline retest, so we can look at the results and the updated packet together.\n"
  },
